            <ArticleTitle>[Early recognition of Churg-Strauss syndrome].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>195-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a patient with Churg-Strauss syndrome which appeared with asthma, chronic sinuitis, peripheral and tissue oeosinophilia, migratory pulmonary infiltrates and polyneuropathy but without histologically proven granuloma or vasculitis. The patient successfully recovered under corticosteroid therapy. The aim of this presentation is early recognition of Churg-Strauss syndrome in order to timely diagnose and treat these patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
